From: Carlos Martins <cjom@reglinux.org>
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: honour OPT_OPENGL and OPT_MT32EMU when probing

Both options already gate the feature defines (C_OPENGL, C_MT32EMU) and
the conditional link generator expressions, but the matching find_package
calls are unconditional and marked REQUIRED. Turning an option off
therefore still fails the configure step on a system that lacks the
library -- the switch only ever removes code, never the requirement.

libdosboxcommon also links OpenGL::GL unconditionally while gating only
libglad next to it, so -DOPT_OPENGL=OFF still needs libGL at link time.
It has it backwards: the render headers include glad/gl.h whatever the
option, so libglad (a runtime loader that needs no libGL) must always be
linked for its include path, and only OpenGL::GL depends on C_OPENGL.

Guard the probes and the link, matching what the meson build allows via
-Duse_opengl=false / -Duse_mt32emu=false. This lets GLES-only targets,
which have no desktop libGL at all, build with -DOPT_OPENGL=OFF.

Signed-off-by: Carlos Martins <cjom@reglinux.org>
---
diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 679470e..8d6208e 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -461,8 +461,12 @@ find_package(SDL2 CONFIG REQUIRED)
 find_package(SDL2_image CONFIG REQUIRED)
 find_package(iir REQUIRED)
 find_package(PNG REQUIRED)
-find_package(OpenGL REQUIRED)
-find_package(MT32Emu REQUIRED)
+if (OPT_OPENGL)
+  find_package(OpenGL REQUIRED)
+endif()
+if (OPT_MT32EMU)
+  find_package(MT32Emu REQUIRED)
+endif()
 find_package(FluidSynth REQUIRED CONFIG)
 if (C_ALSA)
   find_package(ALSA REQUIRED)
diff --git a/src/gui/CMakeLists.txt b/src/gui/CMakeLists.txt
index a1813a0..6500981 100644
--- a/src/gui/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/gui/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -17,5 +17,5 @@ target_sources(libdosboxcommon PRIVATE
 )
 
 target_link_libraries(libdosboxcommon PRIVATE
-  OpenGL::GL
-  $<IF:$<BOOL:${C_OPENGL}>,libglad,>)
+  $<IF:$<BOOL:${C_OPENGL}>,OpenGL::GL,>
+  libglad)
